# The /etc/cfm files the package seeds: "<name> <mode>", one per line.
#
# The .deb seeds them from /usr/share/cfm/configs/ in postinst and never
# overwrites one: an existing file is kept, and a shipped default that differs
# from it lands beside it as <name>.dpkg-dist, the .rpmnew of the rpm's
# %config(noreplace). They are deliberately NOT dpkg conffiles: dpkg stops an
# upgrade to ask about a conffile both sides changed, `apt -y` cannot answer
# it, and unattended-upgrades skips the whole package for it. CFM writes
# several of these files itself (cfm allow / block, the WebUI's notify and
# detectors editors, cfm edge ipv6, cfm kernsec), so that was every node.
#
# The rpm spec's %config(noreplace) list must name the same files
# (scripts/tests/check_deb_config_seed.sh); scripts/tests/ci_seed_cfm_dirs.sh
# seeds CI's /etc/cfm from this list.
cfm.conf 0640
detectors.conf 0640
kernsec.conf 0600
lsm.conf 0600
notify.conf 0640
cfm.allow 0640
cfm.deny 0640
cfm.blocklists 0640
cfm.ignore 0640
cfm.dnat_bypass 0600
cfm.dnat_cpanel_bypass 0600
cfm.dyndns 0640
cfm-admin.htpasswd 0640
webdetector_malpaths.txt 0640
webdetector_challenge_exclude.txt 0640
